# Note: BPE rank files are intentionally NOT tracked with Git LFS.
#
# Earlier this file declared `*.tiktoken filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text`,
# which produced 132-byte LFS pointer files (e.g. `version
# https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1`) in the working tree on machines
# without `git-lfs` installed. The tokenizer then read those pointers
# as if they were BPE dumps and crashed with:
#
#   Failed to load from BPE encoder file stream:
#   Can't parse https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1 to integer
#
# The BPE files actually used at runtime live in
# `@vscode/chat-lib/dist/.../tokenizer/node/` and are copied to
# `dist/{o200k_base,cl100k_base}.tiktoken` by `esbuild.config.js →
# copyBuildAssets()`, then loaded directly via
# `@microsoft/tiktokenizer`'s `createTokenizer(filePath, ...)` (see
# `src/utils/tokenCounter.ts`). Do NOT add `*.tiktoken` back here.
